    "type": "question",
    "label": "52",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following algebraic fractions.\n$$\\frac{\\dfrac8{x+3}}{\\dfrac1{x-3}+\\dfrac2{x^2-9}}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{8(x-3)}{x+5}$, $x\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-5,-3,3\\}$.",
      "worked": "Multiply top and bottom by $x^2-9=(x-3)(x+3)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\frac8{x+3}}{\\frac1{x-3}+\\frac2{x^2-9}}&=\\frac{8(x-3)}{(x+3)+2}\\\\\\frac{\\frac8{x+3}}{\\frac1{x-3}+\\frac2{x^2-9}}&=\\frac{8(x-3)}{x+5}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $x\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-5,-3,3\\}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
